/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The best guess is to fill in the missing values with the mean of the relevant group. Why is this method accurate? Instead of using the mean of the entire column \(which has low accuracy\), we group the data based on other relevant columns \(like Age and Lifestyle\), and then fill the Null values with the mean of that specific group. Example: Assume a patient has a Null value for the LDL \(bad cholesterol\) level.)
/E (The best guess is to fill in the missing values with the mean of the relevant group. Why is this method accurate? Instead of using the mean of the entire column \(which has low accuracy\), we group the data based on other relevant columns \(like Age and Lifestyle\), and then fill the Null values with the mean of that specific group. Example: Assume a patient has a Null value for the LDL \(bad cholesterol\) level.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [0]
>>
